ody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="178" name="Google Shape;178;p19"/><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1" type="body"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="819150" y="2005500"/><a:ext cx="7505700" cy="2448000"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr anchorCtr="0" anchor="t" bIns="91425" lIns="91425" spcFirstLastPara="1" rIns="91425" wrap="square" tIns="91425"><a:noAutofit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr indent="457200" lvl="0" marL="0" rtl="0" algn="l"><a:spcBef><a:spcPts val="0"/></a:spcBef><a:spcAft><a:spcPts val="1600"/></a:spcAft><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>Incase you </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>didn't</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t> know there is more than one type of matter. There are three types of matter: normal matter, antimatter, and dark matter. All are very different and for the most part we hardly know anything about the other two types of matter. Anyways antimatter is the exact opposite of normal matter (as the name suggests). It is made of positrons and antiprotons. Antimatter is the most expensive substance in the world. Jade for example (the 2nd most expensive substance) is $170 million dollars but this is nothing compared to Antimatter. Antimatter is worth about 62.5 trillion dollars for 1 gram. Yes 62.5 trillion. World War 2 for example costed $4 trillion dollars in damages. To make this even crazier Amazon is worth over a trillion dollars which means 1 gram of Antimatter is worth 60x more than Amazon. However, cost </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t>isn't</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en"/><a:t> the only cool fact about Antimatter. Antimatter also destroys normal matter when they touch creating a massive explosion. Antimatter can be used as bombs and only a few grams of it can be powerful enough to destroy massive amounts of land. Antimatter is also being created as we speak. Machines in Sweden called CERN are able to make antimatter but the process is extremely slow. </a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="179" name="Google Shape;179;p19"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId3"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="2959763" y="209563"/><a:ext cx="2619375" cy="1743075"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="180" name="Google Shape;180;p19"/><p:cNvPicPr preferRelativeResize="0"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId4"><a:alphaModFix/></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="6127638" y="260150"/><a:ext cx="2466975" cy="1847850"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/><a:ln><a:noFill/></a:ln></p:spPr></p:pic></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr><mc:AlternateContent><mc:Choice Requires="p14"><p:transition spd="slow" p14:dur="4000"><p:fade/></p:transition></mc:Choice><mc:Fallback><p:transition spd="slow"><p:fade/></p:transition></mc:Fallback></mc:AlternateContent></p:sld>